p.src:
A state with definite momentum $p_0$ satisfies the eigenvalue equation $\hat p_x\psi_{p_0}(x)=p_0\psi_{p_0}(x).$ Substituting the differential form of $\hat p_x$ gives $-i\hbar\frac{d\psi_{p_0}(x)}{dx}
=p_0\psi_{p_0}(x).$ The derivative of the wavefunction is proportional to the wavefunction itself, so the solution has exponential form: $\psi_{p_0}(x)\propto
\exp\left(\frac{ip_0x}{\hbar}\right).$

